<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan's FFC Jordan falls 3.21 pct.</title>
<headline>Pakistan's FFC Jordan falls 3.21 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's FFC Jordan 10-rupee stock fell 0.50 rupee, or 3.21 percent, to 15.10 on Wednesday's new accounts day, Karachi dealers said.</p>
<p>They cited reports that a fertiliser plant FFC Jordan is building near Karachi might not start production until the end of 1998 instead of mid-1998 as scheduled. The reason for the reported delay was not clear and company officials could not immediately be contacted for comment. FFC Jordan is a joint venture with a Jordanian company.</p>
<p>Some 253,000 FFC Jordan shares changed hands in early trade.</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
